From 4978818f4f23cd2d4395908aebd5c388c7997f2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "gastown.slit (polecat)" <polecat-gastown.slit@soundit.local>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 02:37:39 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat: AI asset health score with badge, filter + cached
 explanation (psa-zuj)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Add a 0-100 health score to every asset, shown as a badge in the detail
header and a full breakdown card on the Overview tab, plus a "show
unhealthy assets" filter and Health column on the asset list.

Design (the "what signals + what weights" discussion point):
- The score is DETERMINISTIC and DB-only (no external API calls) — starts
  at 100, each signal subtracts a capped penalty. Fast, auditable, cheap.
- The AI only writes the one-paragraph narrative, never the number; falls
  back to a deterministic paragraph when no AI provider is configured
  (mirrors the triage pipeline's graceful degradation).
- "Unknown is not unhealthy": a signal we can't read contributes nothing.
  With no readable monitoring signal the score is null / grade Unknown,
  not a misleading 100.

Signals & max penalties: connectivity -30, active alerts (by severity,
capped) -40, backup staleness -18, patch/reboot -12, M365 compliance +
Defender -20, open ticket load -10. Grades: >=85 Good, 60-84 Fair, <60
Poor; "unhealthy" filter = Poor.

Caching: score/grade/summary/breakdown cached on the assets table and
refreshed on view only when stale (deterministic; never blocks render on
AI). A background job upgrades the narrative to the AI version after the
page responds. The daily assets:refresh-health command recomputes in bulk
after the overnight vendor syncs and reuses an unchanged AI narrative to
bound AI spend.

- Migration adds health_* columns; AssetHealthGrade enum + AssetHealthResult
  value object; AssetHealthService; RefreshAssetHealth job + command
  (scheduled 06:30); asset-health-badge component.
- Tests: scoring per signal, caps, clamping, unknown handling, cache
  freshness, AI vs deterministic narrative, page render, list filter,
  command. docs/INSTALL.md updated.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
